Plot

library(tidyverse)

water &lt;- read_csv("https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rfordatascience/tidytuesday/main/data/2021/2021-05-04/water.csv")

top_countries &lt;- water |&gt;
  count(country_name, sort = TRUE) |&gt;
  slice_head(n = 8) |&gt;
  pull(country_name)

water |&gt;
  filter(country_name %in% top_countries, !is.na(water_source)) |&gt;
  mutate(water_source = fct_lump_n(water_source, n = 5)) |&gt;
  ggplot(aes(y = fct_infreq(country_name), fill = water_source)) +
  geom_bar(position = "fill") +
  labs(
    x = "Share of recorded water points",
    y = NULL,
    fill = "Water source",
    title = "Water source mix in the eight countries with the most records"
  ) +
  theme_minimal()

How long are movies in each genre?
The duration column is text, so I pulled out the number with the regular expression ^\d+(?= min). The (?= min) part is a lookahead: it matches the digits only when ” min” comes right after them, without keeping ” min” in the result. Each title can be listed under several genres separated by commas, so I used the regular expression ^[^,]+ to keep only the first genre listed.


Code
movies &lt;- netflix |&gt;
  filter(type == "Movie") |&gt;
  mutate(
    minutes = as.numeric(str_extract(duration, "^\\d+(?= min)")),
    main_genre = str_extract(listed_in, "^[^,]+")
  ) |&gt;
  filter(!is.na(minutes))

top_genres &lt;- movies |&gt;
  count(main_genre, sort = TRUE) |&gt;
  slice_head(n = 7) |&gt;
  pull(main_genre)

movies |&gt;
  filter(main_genre %in% top_genres) |&gt;
  mutate(main_genre = fct_reorder(main_genre, minutes, .fun = median)) |&gt;
  ggplot(aes(x = minutes, y = main_genre)) +
  geom_boxplot(fill = "#E8D7B0", outlier.alpha = 0.3) +
  labs(
    x = "Movie length (minutes)",
    y = "First genre listed",
    title = "Dramas and action movies run longest; stand-up specials are shortest",
    subtitle = "Netflix movies in the seven most common genres"
  ) +
  theme_minimal()









Each box shows the middle half of movies in a genre, and the line inside it is the median. Stand-up comedy specials are by far the shortest, with a median of 65 minutes. Children’s movies and documentaries come next at about 86-87 minutes. Dramas and action and adventure movies have the longest median, at 108 minutes. Every genre has long tails, with some movies well over two hours.
